---
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from '../../../i18n/utils';

const t = useTranslations(getLangFromUrl(Astro.url));
---

<p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
    A few years ago I discovered a game for learning programming:
    <a
        href="https://codecombat.com/user/cararcel"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">CodeCombat</a
    >. I started playing for fun and learned a lot. Then I decided to take some
    courses to dive deeper. The first ones were on
    <a
        href="https://laracasts.com/"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Laracasts</a
    >. I watched videos on HTML, CSS, and PHP. Jeffrey Way explains things very
    well; everything looks simple, and I was behind the screen trying to figure
    out why it didn’t work for me (spoiler alert: sometimes it was just a typo).
</p>

<p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
    Later I discovered
    <a
        href="https://grafikart.fr"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Grafikart</a
    >, which was great for me because I could practice my French (at least
    understand it) while continuing to learn. I revisited HTML and CSS and kept
    going with JavaScript.
</p>

<p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
    Deciding to go back to school (officially) was tough, but I wanted to
    formalize the knowledge I already had and keep learning more about web
    development. So I enrolled in a career‑change program at
    <a
        href="https://openclassrooms.com/fr/paths/899-developpeur-web"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">OpenClassrooms</a
    >. Now I can say I am
    <a
        href="/assets/oc-certificat.pdf"
        title="my OpenClassrooms certificate"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline"
    >
        officially a web developer.
    </a>Hoorray!!
</p>

<p class="text-lg text-justify text-black leading-8 tracking-wide mb-8">
    After finishing my training I devoted myself to motherhood and personal
    projects that keep me up‑to‑date (or at least prevent my skills from
    rusting). Currently I’m learning more about React through the
    <a
        href="https://www.epicreact.dev/"
        target="_blank"
        class="font-bold underline hover:no-underline">Epic React</a
    >
    course.
</p>
